 "license": "The repository states no licence for its data or prose. GitHub reports MIT from BOUND_VERIFIER_LICENSE.txt, which is Evan Daniel's licence for the verifier verify_bound_certificate.py ('modifications by Francisco Couzo with Codex'); both are byte-identical to the copies the couzo-issue678-2026-10-18 packet retains and are pinned against them. Francisco Couzo submitted this source to the repository in issue #763, and the owner ruled on 24 October 2026 that a source its author submitted carries a presumption of permission to retain and import it (think-cnn7); the exact licence is followed up on think-m8f4 without holding the import. The certificates, indexes, README and construction checker are retained on that presumption, and the certificates are factual data under the owner decision of 2026-10-09 as well (resources/web/known-best-packings/README.md, Retained Factual Data). The presumption covers Couzo's own material only. The 87 notebook certificates added for think-lyf9 are the packings of other authors' Kaggle notebooks, and are retained as factual data under the owner decision of 2026-10-09, as the 268 parent is; the manifest states Apache-2.0 for the notebooks of 28 of them and 'per the notebook' for 59, and the SOURCE_NOTICES.md it cites is not in the tree at 964ee2b. Those licences are followed up on think-m8f4 and hold nothing. The 103 certificates added for #795's review A are factual data under the same decision: 76 are sides the index states as Couzo's own at efef7d1 and fa6237e, retained on the presumption as well, one, the root certificate at 994, is a side the index credits to Polkovskyi, which restates his earlier side, and 26 are notebook packings, Tymchishin's v3 (16), Lavrentev's v11 (9) and the 859 recipe of Lavrentev's run 361589987 (1), whose licences think-m8f4 follows up as for the 87. The provenance review, per-count provenance and the certificate catalogue's README and digest list are pinned by digest only, as are the parents' README and manifest.",
 "claims": [
  "Issue #763 asks to register 436 improved upper bounds, 203 at or below 1024 and 233 above, selected from certified_bounds.json at 964ee2b by the README's rule (a count credited to Couzo whose exact certified side, rounded up at 12 places, is strictly below the reviewed comparison's print where that comparison is his own, and more than 1e-10 below it where it is another author's), with exact certificate headers authoritative. The issue carries no table; devtools.couzo_763_claims re-derives the 436 from the retained indexes (receipts/claim-map.json): 196 certificate rows (194 own-count certificates and the deletions 683 and 1646), 239 tiling and L-border recipes and the recipe deletion 1727.",
